# Writing / reviewing MALDA source

Before generating or substantially editing `.malda` files:

1. Read `docs/llm/malda-syntax.md` and `docs/llm/malda-gotchas.md`
2. Pull 1–3 matching snippets from `docs/llm/few-shot/` or `Examples/`
3. If unsure about syntax, check `docs/llm/malda-grammar.md`
4. Do not invent builtins — grep `docs/llm/malda-builtins.tsv`; absence from it is authoritative

Style:

- Use `function` (`fn`/`def` are syntax errors)
- Prompt params are name-only (no `name: string`)
- Call the stdlib through its namespace: `math.sqrt`, `str.upper`, `io.print`. Flat and `Math.` spellings raise style warnings
- No string interpolation outside prompt bodies — concatenate with `+ string(x)`
- Verify with `dotnet run --project MaldaLang -- path/to/file.malda` when practical. For interactive or random programs, `math.seed(n)` plus a piped stdin transcript makes the run deterministic
